WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:06.359
All spruced up and ready for a new
tenant. The Waimakariri District Council

00:00:06.359 --> 00:00:10.559
has recently renovated two of its
pensioner housing units as part of a

00:00:10.559 --> 00:00:15.660
pilot scheme.  It's more than just a lick
of paint the remodeled units boast

00:00:15.660 --> 00:00:19.020
new carpet, kitchens, laundries and double glazing throughout.

00:00:19.020 --> 00:00:24.800
Some even have dedicated
parking and charging spots for mobility scooters.

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:29.960
I think it's very impressive
and it's in modern colors and it looks warm

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:33.900
and inviting. It's really good to see
this upgrade

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:39.760
Not only are they more attractive, Jean Gouedard from the Council's property team says the newly improved

00:00:39.760 --> 00:00:43.860
units will save tenants money on their
power bill and be healthier to live in.

00:00:44.540 --> 00:00:51.360
We are really encouraging our residents
to have healthier living and with the

00:00:51.360 --> 00:00:58.020
insulation and all the functionality of
the kitchen and everything, we hope that

00:00:58.020 --> 00:01:03.460
they'll have nicer living conditions and you'd be proud to have anyone here.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:06.540
These units are part of
the Council's pensioner housing

00:01:06.540 --> 00:01:11.400
facility in Kaiapoi's Martyn Place and
were first built in the late 60s.

00:01:11.840 --> 00:01:15.520
They were due for a makeover
however originally only the kitchens

00:01:15.520 --> 00:01:16.880
were going to be replaced.

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:21.040
Because we needed the removal of asbestos, it was a

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:26.160
good idea to do more than just the
kitchen fit out so that we could update

00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:34.160
all the insulation throughout including
double glazing for windows and doors.

00:01:34.800 --> 00:01:38.400
Modern building code requirements mean
that the units require reinvestment

00:01:38.430 --> 00:01:43.110
if they're to remain safe and functional for
the next 50 years. If the pilot scheme is

00:01:43.120 --> 00:01:46.640
successful and approved by Council as
part of the Long Term Plan,

00:01:46.640 --> 00:01:51.119
similar improvements will be rolled out for Council pensioner housing district-wide.

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.979
That would require a rental increase for
tenants, however this would largely be

00:01:56.000 --> 00:02:00.560
offset by government housing subsidies
and reduced energy and medical bills.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:06.400
We've got over a hundred units across
Woodend, Oxford, Rangiora and Kaiapoi

00:02:06.400 --> 00:02:11.430
and most of them are fairly old and so
refurbishing them and bringing them up to

00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:13.760
modern standards, I think is very
important for the residents.

00:02:14.720 --> 00:02:19.350
Council will be considering the plan later this year and if approved, the renovations

00:02:19.360 --> 00:02:22.240
will be rolled out over the next five to
ten years

